<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23196" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαί</span></b> , colloquial form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δή,</span> used after interrogatives, to express wonder or
		curiosity, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς δ. ὅμιλος ὅδ᾽ ἔπλετο;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.225
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῦ δ. νηῦς ἕστηκε;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.299
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				78.2
			</span></i> (but wrongly read by <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> for 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ᾽ αἱ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.408
				</span></i>
			): freq. in Com., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δ. σὺ . . πεποίηκας;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					351
				</span></i>
			; mostly in a separate clause, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίδ.;</span>”
				<i>what? how?</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					93
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				171
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δ. σύ;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Av.</u>
					136
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶς δ.;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>V.</u>
					1212
				</span></i>
			; dub. l. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				933
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				900
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				318
			</span></i>, but prob. to be read <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1012
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ion</u>
				275
			</span></i>, al.: freq. in codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i>, but prob. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέ</span>
			, as in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				912
			</span></i>.</div>
